\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Bar\'92s in the left tent, fireworks in the right,\'94 the bouncer said, with the bored ambivalence of someone who\'92d already tasered three customers before lunch.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A pair of catherine wheels ricocheted by, trailing smoke and near-deafening Hayley. She caught herself, muttering that Friday nights weren\'92t what they used to be, and scanned for anyone who might be Chantara\'92s friends.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Picnic chairs in the scorched median, a battered card table littered with noisy beers and illegal explosives\'97and there they were. One, a pirate by the look of his hat and a silver hoop in his ear, double-fisted his lager while monitoring the crowd with cash-register eyes. The other, a fence if ever she\'92d seen one, slick suit, shades at dusk, habitually checking his phone as if it were bonded evidence.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She approached, badge pocketed for now. \'93Excuse me, do you know Anthony Chantara?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Who, luv?\'94 the pirate grunted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are you his date?\'94 the fence asked, eyeing her sidelong.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No. Just looking for Tony\'85 Chanta,\'94 Hayley replied, careful.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Oh, Chanta! Why didn\'92t you say so?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yeah, everyone knows Chanta!\'94 the pirate crowed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Before they could ramble, Hayley said, \'93Have you heard about his arrest? There\'92s some serious accusations out there\'97bombing, kidnapping, murder.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The pirate sucked his teeth. \'93He never did any of those things.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Why do you say that?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Not enough wattage up top. Cleaning\'92s his high watermark,\'94 said the pirate, tapping his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He does the jobs even bots can\'92t do,\'94 chimed the fence, raising his glass.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Robot cleaners, mate,\'94 said the pirate, shaking his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sure... nothing scrubs a bog like Chanta. I\'92ve seen a cleaning bot with PTSD after cleaning a toilet bowl\'85 say, after a big night out the last thing you do before you pass out it you bring up a gallon of beer and that rancid kebab you should never have had. And in the morning it\'92s all there, drying and sticking\'85.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I once went out with a woman who never used the toilet.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Never used the toilet?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I mean for being sick in. She threw up in the sink.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re kidding.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, I swear. Now, I\'92ll tell you, a bathroom sink full of fetid peas and carrots in the morning is a tough clean-up.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Anyway, Chanta\'92s no criminal,\'94 the fence saluted. \'93He\'92s just this guy, you know?\'97the one you call when you need miracles.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

